WEBVTT

00:00:00.015 --> 00:00:02.823
Easy Science. What Is a Rainbow?

00:00:02.823 --> 00:00:06.700
A rainbow is one of the most beautiful things in the sky.

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:11.909
To see one, you need two things at the same time: sun and rain.

00:00:11.909 --> 00:00:15.639
Sunlight looks white, but it is made of many colors.

00:00:15.639 --> 00:00:21.378
Most of the time these colors travel together, and we cannot see them one by one.

00:00:21.378 --> 00:00:24.278
A drop of rain can pull the colors apart.

00:00:24.278 --> 00:00:29.097
When sunlight goes into a drop of water, the light bends a little.

00:00:29.097 --> 00:00:32.807
Then it hits the back of the drop and comes out again.

00:00:32.807 --> 00:00:35.495
Each color bends by a different amount.

00:00:35.495 --> 00:00:39.400
So the colors leave the drop in slightly different directions.

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:47.074
When the sun shines on millions of raindrops at once, we see the colors spread across the sky in a wide curve.

00:00:47.074 --> 00:00:49.437
Red is always on the outside.

00:00:49.437 --> 00:00:51.795
Purple is always on the inside.

00:00:51.795 --> 00:00:57.373
To see a rainbow, you must stand with the sun behind you and the rain in front of you.

00:00:57.373 --> 00:01:02.850
That is why we often see rainbows late in the afternoon, just after a storm.

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:06.028
No two people see exactly the same rainbow.

00:01:06.028 --> 00:01:09.929
The light reaches each person's eyes from different raindrops.

00:01:09.929 --> 00:01:12.830
So the rainbow you see belongs only to you.
